    "result_text": "Green. Done.\n\n## What I changed\n\nI agreed with the one structural finding \u2014 the daily-count predicate was duplicated verbatim across `FlagBulkSignup` and `RejectOverDailyLimit` \u2014 and factored it into a single home:\n\n- **New `OwnerDailyCount`** (package-private, final, non-instantiable) with `sharingRegistrationDate(repo, date)` holding the one copy of the \"owners sharing this registration date\" scan.\n- **`RejectOverDailyLimit`** and **`FlagBulkSignup`** now both call that helper, each keeping only its own threshold constant (`100` reject / `80` warn) and terminal action (throw vs. set flag). Removed the now-unused `LocalDate` imports.\n\nI deliberately did **not** take the `Out<Long>`/`@Qualifier` sharing route the review listed first: it would couple `FlagBulkSignup` to `RejectOverDailyLimit` having run and published a variable earlier in the pipeline, trading verbatim duplication for an ordering/wiring dependency between two otherwise-independent rules \u2014 against the codebase's self-contained-step habit. The helper removes the maintained-in-two-places predicate without that coupling. (I left `CountOwnerNamesakes` untouched, since the review correctly notes it scans on a genuinely different predicate.)\n\nAcceptance behaviour is unchanged and the suite passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
